(7677805, 1255400, 30049, '<td valign="top">FYI - This was my top pick for the challenge.  Glad it still made top 10, but very surprised not to see it at the top of the order.  Wonderful portrait.</td>', 'FYI - This was my top pick for the challenge.  Glad it still made top 10, but very surprised not to see it at the top of the order.  Wonderful portrait.', '2020-10-26 07:43:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7677806, 1255407, 30049, '<td valign="top">Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc.</td>', 'Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc.', '2020-10-26 07:46:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7677808, 1255407, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment. I am confused how you guessed my editing process on this photo. I did not apply any blur at all to this image. I actually did very little processing and it was essentially a crop, and desaturation and a touch of selective sharpening of the stag.</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc.   Thank you for your comment. I am confused how you guessed my editing process on this photo. I did not apply any blur at all to this image. I actually did very little processing and it was essentially a crop, and desaturation and a touch of selective sharpening of the stag.', '2020-10-26 08:39:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7677812, 1255401, 104230, '<td valign="top">Wonderful. Great work with the extremes of tonal range, and lovely lighting and focus. I gave it one of my few 8s.</td>', 'Wonderful. Great work with the extremes of tonal range, and lovely lighting and focus. I gave it one of my few 8s.', '2020-10-26 09:10:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7677813, 1255421, 104230, '<td valign="top">.. what <img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=69668" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">njsabs</a> said and I love the wide angle perspective. I gave it one of the my few 8s.</td>', '.. what  njsabs said and I love the wide angle perspective. I gave it one of the my few 8s.', '2020-10-26 09:16:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7677814, 1255407, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment. I am confused how you guessed my editing process on this photo. I did not apply any blur at all to this image. I actually did very little processing and it was essentially a crop, and desaturation and a touch of selective sharpening of the stag. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Well DANG there slim jim lens man!  That''s a super slim slice for F8!  Ok, I stand corrected and I''m eating crow.  Pretty cool, and thanks for sharing.</td>', 'Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Originally posted by glad2badad: Don''t take this the wrong way  the detail on the bull is fantastic, but I''m shocked that this made Top 10 with the amount of selective blur applied.  It kind of looks like a toy figure with the current presentation - not that dissimilar to the miniature effect with tilt shift or selective blur on an elevated cityscape, etc.   Thank you for your comment. I am confused how you guessed my editing process on this photo. I did not apply any blur at all to this image. I actually did very little processing and it was essentially a crop, and desaturation and a touch of selective sharpening of the stag.  Well DANG there slim jim lens man!  That''s a super slim slice for F8!  Ok, I stand corrected and I''m eating crow.  Pretty cool, and thanks for sharing.', '2020-10-26 09:20:44.000000', NULL, 0),
